xual misconduct after being  reported to the parliamentary watchdog  this is in the sunday times today among  they say 56 mps have been referred in  total  i mean how concerned are you and what  does it say about the culture at  westminster  if this is happening  well  on the face of it those look like  concerning allegations but i think you'd  expect that due process should happen  and that the investigation should be  conducted i i personally know absolutely  nothing about it and you wouldn't expect  me to that be a matter for anything for  house authorities culture at westminster  do you think that westminster is a safe  place to be a woman  yes i do think it's a safe place to be  and i think actually we've made uh big  improvements over the past uh 20 or 30  years and some of the the things that  happened i'm sure when you were a young  reporter when i started out in  westminster certainly wouldn't happen  now and i think that's that's something  that has improved very much for the  better okay just finally while i have  you um you said in the speech back in  february that woke ideology  is a dangerous form of decadence  what what exactly does that mean  well what it means is i think yeah i  grew up  uh under thatcher and churchill and uh  previous gender so that  reagan forgive me other generations of  church  that would be that would be something  i'd be particularly youthful looking  other generations grew up under  roosevelt and uh and churchill and we we  fundamentally believe that we were the  good guys in history we stood for  freedom speech democracy rule of law and  and so on i think this work ideology  turns out on its head and that she says  well this is this is my point this is  this this movement emanating i think  beginning from the hard lift  increasingly creeping more broadly that  says actually that's not the right  narrative the reality is our history is  one of uh misogyny of racism of  exploitation and i think that's actually  something that 